🔐 Task 4 – Penetration Testing Workflow

ApexPlanet Software Pvt. Ltd.

📌 Overview

This repository documents Task 4, completed as part of my cybersecurity learning program with ApexPlanet Software Pvt. Ltd.
The task focuses on understanding and implementing the Penetration Testing Methodology in a controlled lab environment.

⚠️ All activities were performed ethically on authorized test systems only (Metasploitable2).

🎯 Objective

Learn the complete penetration testing workflow

Exploit known vulnerabilities responsibly

Understand password attacks, social engineering (simulation), malware basics

Apply system hardening techniques

Document findings and mitigations professionally

🧠 Penetration Testing Phases Covered
1️⃣ Reconnaissance

Network discovery

Target identification

2️⃣ Scanning & Enumeration

Port scanning (Nmap)

Service and vulnerability detection

3️⃣ Exploitation

Exploiting known vulnerabilities in Metasploitable2

Gaining access using Metasploit

Establishing a reverse shell

4️⃣ Post-Exploitation

System information gathering

Password hash dumping

Privilege verification

5️⃣ Password Attacks

SSH brute-force using Hydra

Password hash cracking using John the Ripper

6️⃣ Social Engineering (Simulation Only)

Phishing awareness simulation

Understanding human-based attack vectors

Defensive awareness training

7️⃣ Malware Basics

Static vs Dynamic malware analysis

Sandbox-based benign sample analysis

8️⃣ System Hardening

Applying security patches

Firewall configuration

Disabling unused services

Reducing attack surface

🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used

Kali Linux

Metasploitable2

Nmap

Metasploit Framework

Hydra

John the Ripper

Netcat

Linux Firewall (UFW)

